.\" does not need it: mdxfind carries the site key as an ordinary salt and emits
.\" TYPE record:sitekey:plaintext, so a pipe or saved solution file already holds
.\" the key, and an inline key is the only one tried. -j answers a line with no key
.\" of its own and is consulted only under -c. Records that the file is read at
.\" start-up and that an unopenable name, an empty file, an odd-length $HEX[]
.\" payload or an over-long key is fatal there, because each would otherwise surface
.\" as nothing verified, which for an encrypted record is indistinguishable from a
.\" wrong key; and that a record reaching the verifier with no key from either
.\" channel is named UNSATISFIABLE rather than counted as a failed password. Traced
